.TH "PKGSTATE\-CHECK" "1" "" "libpkgstate\-posix" "Version 3.1.0"
.SH NAME
pkgstate\-check \- validate and summarize native installed state
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]pkgstate\-check\f[R] \f[B]\-\-canonical\-store\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]\-\-managed\-target\f[R] \f[I]identity\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]\-\-state\-store\f[R] \f[I]identity\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]\-\-root\-view\f[R] \f[I]identity\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]\-\-state\-backend\f[R] \f[I]identity\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]\-\-publication\-domain\f[R] \f[I]identity\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.PP
\f[B]pkgstate\-check\f[R] {\f[B]\-V\f[R] | \f[B]\-h\f[R]}
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]pkgstate\-check\f[R] opens an existing canonical generation store, validates its binding and selected generation, and prints one complete report.
The command is read\-only.
It does not initialize a missing store, repair records, publish a generation, execute lifecycle programs, or import another package database.
.SH OPTIONS
\f[B]\-c\f[R], \f[B]\-\-canonical\-store\f[R]=\f[I]path\f[R] Inspect the existing generation store at \f[I]path\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]\-\-managed\-target\f[R]=\f[I]identity\f[R] Expected managed\-target identity.
.PP
\f[B]\-\-state\-store\f[R]=\f[I]identity\f[R] Expected durable state\-store identity.
.PP
\f[B]\-\-root\-view\f[R]=\f[I]identity\f[R] Expected logical target root\-view identity.
.PP
\f[B]\-\-state\-backend\f[R]=\f[I]identity\f[R] Expected state\-backend identity.
.PP
\f[B]\-\-publication\-domain\f[R]=\f[I]identity\f[R] Expected publication\-domain identity.
.PP
\f[B]\-V\f[R], \f[B]\-\-version\f[R] Print version and exit.
.PP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\-\-help\f[R] Print usage and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
The report includes storage format, target binding, snapshot and ownership identities, package and ownership counts, rejected\-object references, and package counts by installation reason.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 The store is valid and the report was emitted.
.PP
1 The store or binding is invalid.
.PP
2 Command\-line usage is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
